# Story 45: PTY Resize (40s)
# Hook: Resize the window and your programs follow -- SIGWINCH propagates and the emulator reflows.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-045-pty-resize.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Resize the window and your programs follow -- SIGWINCH propagates and the emulator reflows.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and check the terminal dimensions.

[00:08.0 --> 00:15.0]
Run tput to read the current columns and rows -- the values the PTY is reporting to your shell.

[00:15.0 --> 00:23.0]
Split a pane with Ctrl+P n. Splitting changes each pane's geometry, and Rysh sends a SIGWINCH so the shell learns its new size.

[00:23.0 --> 00:30.0]
Check again in the narrower pane -- the column count has dropped. The PTY was resized live, no restart needed.

[00:30.0 --> 00:37.0]
Interactive programs adapt too. Launch htop -- the vt10x emulator reflows its layout to whatever space the pane currently has.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Resize freely. Your shells and full-screen apps reflow to fit.

